    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 261 tests pass \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented soft-duplicate detection for `POST /api/owners` so that a new owner sharing an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` but with a *different* telephone is still created and flagged.\n\n**How it works:** a hard duplicate (exact identity-key match on telephone/email/household) is already rejected upstream by `EnsureOwnerIdentityUnique`. Since a soft match has a *different* telephone, its identity key differs, so it always passes that check \u2014 this new step then flags it rather than rejecting.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`AssignPossibleDuplicate.java`** (new function) \u2014 after `BuildOwner`/`NormalizeOwnerTelephone`, scans existing owners for one with the same last name (case-insensitive) and same postcode but a different telephone. Sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf`=the matching owner id (lowest id when several qualify, for determinism); otherwise `possibleDuplicate=false`.\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the step into the pipeline (after `assignNamesakeCount`, before `assignMembershipLevel`, under the same `transaction` governance) so the flag is persisted with the new row and read back by `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n3. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 two persisted columns (`possible_duplicate`, `possible_duplicate_of`) with getters/setters.\n\n4. **Schema SQL** (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres) \u2014 added the two columns to the `owners` table.\n\n5. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32) as read-only fields on the `Owner` schema; MapStruct auto-maps them by name into `OwnerDto`, so no mapper change was needed.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate` and the entire existing suite are green.",
